Subject: [PATCH] riscv_pcie_soc: write ram from always, not always_ff

ram is initialised by `$readmemh` in an initial block and written by
an always_ff. IEEE 1800-2017 9.2.2.4 forbids any other process writing
a variable assigned in always_ff; VCS rejects the file with
Error-[ICPD]. `always` removes the restriction with no change in
simulation or synthesis behaviour.

Found by the openpcie-uvm Tier 1 testbench (RTL-SIM-001); see
docs/verification_plan.md, section 11, in that repository.

---
--- a/2.rtl/2.RC-direct.opensource/src/riscv_pcie_soc.sv
+++ b/2.rtl/2.RC-direct.opensource/src/riscv_pcie_soc.sv
@@ -103,7 +103,9 @@
     logic [31:0] ram_rdata_reg;
     logic        ram_ready_reg;
 
-    always_ff @(posedge clk) begin
+    // `ram` is also written by the $readmemh above, which IEEE 1800-2017
+    // 9.2.2.4 forbids for a variable assigned in always_ff.
+    always @(posedge clk) begin
         ram_ready_reg <= 1'b0;
         if (mem_valid && is_ram) begin
             if (mem_wstrb == '0) begin
